---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import JsonToCsv from '../../components/JsonToCsv.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="JSON to CSV Converter" description="Convert a JSON array of objects into a downloadable CSV, instantly in your browser.">
  <JsonToCsv client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>Paste a JSON array of flat objects. The tool collects all unique keys across every object as CSV headers, so it handles arrays with inconsistent fields gracefully.</p>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Using deeply nested JSON</strong> that doesn't map cleanly to flat CSV columns — flatten nested objects first for a cleaner conversion.</li>
    <li><strong>Not checking for inconsistent fields across objects</strong>, which can leave some CSV cells empty if not every object has every field.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Exporting API response data to a spreadsheet-friendly format</li>
    <li>Converting a JSON dataset for import into Excel or Google Sheets</li>
    <li>Preparing JSON data for a system that only accepts CSV input</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
